        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entra" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Microsoft Entra ID&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;App registration, groups,&lt;br&gt;storage consent&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1460" y="110" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entra-icon" parent="entra" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pipeline" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Delivery pipeline&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;GitHub or Azure DevOps&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1460" y="495" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pipeline-icon" parent="pipeline" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="email" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Email recipients&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#5c5c5c&quot;&gt;Alert receivers&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;verticalAlign=top;arcSize=12;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#8a8781;dashed=1;dashPattern=5 4;spacingTop=37;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="660" y="870" width="200" height="80" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="email-icon" parent="email" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/svg+xml,;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="88.0" y="11" width="24" height="24" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-files" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;File access: what the page does and why&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sign-in:&lt;/b&gt; Static Web Apps built-in authentication opens the site for allowed Entra groups only. files.js then uses MSAL.js (pinned copy 3.28.1, integrity-checked) to get the user&amp;#x27;s own token for Azure Storage, silently when the session exists.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Calls:&lt;/b&gt; list, upload, download and delete go from the browser straight to the blob endpoint. Private DNS resolves it to the storage private endpoint. CORS allows only the site&amp;#x27;s own origins, and the content security policy allows connections only to this account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why this way:&lt;/b&gt; no API or server code, no account key anywhere, and every blob operation in the logs carries the real user.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt; the allowed groups hold a custom role on the files container: read, write, delete and blob-tag read.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Recovery:&lt;/b&gt; versioning and soft delete keep replaced and deleted files for 7 days in dev and qa, 14 in uat and 30 in prod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Malware:&lt;/b&gt; Defender for Storage scans uploads in uat and prod; a flagged file gets a blob tag and the page hides it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does not prove:&lt;/b&gt; that a user cannot skip the page&amp;#x27;s file type and size limits by calling storage with their own token, or that a file is clean in the seconds before its scan finishes." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="985" width="800" height="240" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-plain" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;How people share files, and how it is watched&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What happens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A colleague on the corporate network opens the site and signs in with their APEX account&lt;br&gt;• On the Files page they see everything in the library, and can add, replace, download or delete a file&lt;br&gt;• The files never leave the private network: the page talks to Azure storage straight from the colleague&amp;#x27;s own browser&lt;br&gt;• A replaced or deleted file can still be brought back by an operator for a few weeks&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why we do it this way&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• There is no extra server to run, patch or pay for&lt;br&gt;• Nobody holds a shared password or key for the files: each person uses their own sign-in, so the logs show who did what&lt;br&gt;• In production, uploads are scanned for malware" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="860" y="985" width="800" height="240" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-mind" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;What to keep in mind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Depends on:&lt;/b&gt; the platform team for hub peering and for corporate DNS to resolve the privatelink zones, including privatelink.blob.core.windows.net.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;One-time step:&lt;/b&gt; an Entra admin must consent to the Azure Storage permission on the app registration, or every user is asked.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Weak links:&lt;/b&gt; everyone assigned can overwrite or delete any file. The type and size limits are checked in the browser only. The storage token lives in the browser, so the page&amp;#x27;s scripts are locked down and MSAL.js is a pinned copy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt; only from the corporate network. In the Azure portal, operators need a role and private access to browse files, because account keys are off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Limits:&lt;/b&gt; Static Web Apps regions only. One upload request per file, sized for the default 100 MB, not for multi-gigabyte files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cost:&lt;/b&gt; about $38 a month per environment in dev and qa (ZRS, no scanning) and about $46 in uat and prod (GZRS, scanning), for 100 GB stored. Storage is $0.024 per GB in ZRS and $0.046 in GZRS; scanning is $0.15 per GB uploaded. Budgets are 100, 150, 200 and 300.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Status:&lt;/b&gt; validated and tested with mocked providers only; not yet applied to Azure and the page not yet run against real storage." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="1255" width="800" height="290" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-why" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Why pick this design, and its trade-offs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Browser to Blob, not an API:&lt;/b&gt; no code or compute to run, and the logs show the real user. Trade-off: file checks run only in the browser, and the browser holds a storage token.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No account keys, not shared keys:&lt;/b&gt; nothing to leak or rotate. Trade-off: operators need a role and private access to browse files in the portal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;One shared library, not per-user folders:&lt;/b&gt; simple to understand and audit. Trade-off: anyone assigned can delete anyone&amp;#x27;s file; versioning and soft delete make that recoverable, not impossible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Custom container role, not Storage Blob Data Contributor:&lt;/b&gt; the built-in role cannot read blob tags, which the malware check needs. Trade-off: one more resource to keep right.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Versioning and soft delete, not backups:&lt;/b&gt; a mistaken overwrite or delete is undone by an operator. Trade-off: old versions are billed until they expire, and there is no undo button on the page.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Malware scanning on in uat and prod, off in dev and qa:&lt;/b&gt; shared files are where malware can enter. Trade-off: a per-account and per-GB charge, and a file is downloadable until its scan completes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ZRS in dev and qa, GZRS in uat and prod:&lt;/b&gt; zone and region resilience where it matters. Trade-off: GZRS costs about twice as much per GB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Private endpoint and Entra sign-in, not a public site:&lt;/b&gt; every user is internal, so there is no internet entry to defend. Trade-off: no access off the corporate network, and a dependency on hub and DNS." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="860" y="1255" width="800" height="290" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e0" parent="1" value="HTTPS" style="html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;endFill=1;strokeColor=#3f3f52;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;endArrow=classic;endSize=6;jettySize=auto;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.85;entryY=0;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" source="user" target="hub">
